---
title: "Confirm a phone number verification"
icon: pencil
description: "Confirm a phone number verification: confirmAccountPhoneVerification in the TypeScript, Python and Rust clients."
---

`PUT /v1/account/phone`

Binds the number once the code is approved. Repeat calls return the bound Account.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.account.confirmPhoneVerification(input: ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.account.confirm_phone_verification(input: ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationInput) -> models.Account
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.confirm_account_phone_verification(body: &types::ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationRequest).await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::Account>, Error<ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.account.confirmPhoneVerification({
  body: {
    code: "code",
    phoneNumber: "phoneNumber",
  },
});
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon
from photon_api.rpc_generated import ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationInput

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.account.confirm_phone_verification(
    ConfirmAccountPhoneVerificationInput.model_validate({
        "body": {
            "code": "code",
            "phoneNumber": "phoneNumber",
        },
    })
)
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .confirm_account_phone_verification(
        &serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
            "code": "code",
            "phoneNumber": "phoneNumber",
        }))?,
    )
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

